        # THE DOCK FACE. /World/Architecture/Dock/SlabFront2 and SlabFront3 - the
        # 1.2 m high cast face that closes DETAIL_WET_APRON at 15.1 m, and the single
        # surface three review rounds have called a flat blue-grey plate.
        #
        # It is now BOARD-FORMED concrete, not a wall scan. conrete_formed_diff is
        # four horizontal shutter-board bands per tile with a proud lip at each board
        # joint, which is what a cast-in-situ dock face actually is and what the
        # critic's "no form-tie marks, one faint panel line" is asking for; the tile
        # below works out to 2.4 m across and 1.2 m down, i.e. FOUR 0.30 m boards
        # over the exact height of the face, with the joints landing where the
        # formwork's would. On top of it _mat_tune puts spongy_concrete_dirt_mask as
        # the second albedo layer - a real vertical wash mask, so the staining runs
        # down the face under gravity - and drives roughness off the same mask, so a
        # dark run is also a wet one and picks the sky up specularly.
