    # ======================================================================
    # DRUM LOOK OVERRIDES  ->  /World/Props/Looks/D_*
    # ======================================================================
    # 30_props authors these fifteen looks and binds them to 295 drums with
    # bindMaterialAs = "strongerThanDescendants". 50_materials is the stronger
    # sublayer, so the `over` prims below replace the SHADER on each of them
    # without touching one binding, one transform or one prim in 30_props.
    #
    # WHY. They were vMaterials presets at texture_scale 0.52-0.66. Measured on
    # the asset: steeldrum_a01's primvars:st is a uniform 2.0000 metres of
    # surface per uv unit on all four submeshes (body, cover, rim, detail), so
    # those numbers put a 3.0-3.8 m texture tile on a 0.868 m drum - a quarter
    # of one repeat across the whole prop, which magnifies to a single flat
    # value. On screen: a clean glossy jet-black cylinder with one specular
    # band, and two flat cream cylinders.
    #
    # WHAT CHANGED. OmniPBR driven by explicit vMaterials texture URLs (the
    # same route that already works for the 94 OmniPBR looks in this layer, so
    # MDL resolution is no longer a variable), world cubic projection, a
    # 0.22-0.38 m base tile and a second 0.038-0.060 m detail normal. World
    # projection also means every one of the 295 drums samples a different
    # region of the map, so no two are the same drum.
